Usage: aranum <subcommand> [args...]

Examples:
  aranum run scan01 -report --session-name acme   # generates artifacts, non-blocking
  aranum run scan01 -serve  --session-name acme   # also serves the dashboard (blocks)
  aranum iter --session-name acme
  aranum dashboard               # newest outputs/<session>/raw + reports/dashboard

Output layout:
  outputs/<session>/raw      raw scanner/dispatcher output
  outputs/<session>/inputs   derived inputs: hosts, users, scope, loot
  outputs/<session>/reports  report.md/html/json and dashboard files

Subcommands:
  bulk-linux, bulk-windows, dashboard, deps-check, export-recce, iter, merge, plan, queue, report, run, selftest, ssh-key-triage, ssh-triage, version
  - bulk-linux: bash bulk-enum-linux.sh
  - bulk-windows: python bulk-enum-windows.py
  - dashboard: wrapper for report-dashboard.py with safe defaults
  - deps-check: run deps-check.sh — verify enumeration tooling
  - export-recce: python aranum_to_recce.py
  - iter: bash iterative-enum.sh
  - merge: python merge-results.py
  - plan: python plan.py
  - queue: built-in queue viewer
  - report: python report.py
  - run: bash auto-enum.sh; -report chains report + dashboard (non-blocking), -serve also serves it
  - selftest: run the smoke.sh self-test suite
  - ssh-key-triage: python ssh-key-triage.py
  - ssh-triage: bash ssh-triage.sh
  - version: print the aranum version (also: aranum --version)
